  "details": "The 3rd person camera looks great at a distance but as you zoom in it weirdly sits mid-screen and appears to be centered on the viewpoint. This results in the avatar appearing at the bottom of the screen rather than in frame like most 3rd person games have with over-the-shoulder views.\n\nCurrently the avatar sits roughly at the bottom 3rd of the screen or lower depending on zoom. Having the camera either adjustable or centered a bit lower as you zoom in so that the avatar covers about 2/3rds of the screen would feel a lot more natural. (included screenshot with drawing illustrating what I'm talking about)\n\nHaving the ability to adjust the height to preference would be ideal to accommodate all avatars or avatars with strange forms as well.",
